  "title": "Why Boundaries Create Safety",
  "content": "Boundaries are not about control—they are about safety, predictability, and emotional security. Children feel safer when they know what is expected and how adults will respond. Without boundaries, children may feel overwhelmed, confused, or anxious because the world feels unpredictable.\n\nMany parents struggle with boundaries because they were raised with either harsh discipline or no boundaries at all. This lesson reframes boundaries as an act of care, not punishment. Boundaries help children learn self‑control, responsibility, and respect for others.\n\nWhen boundaries are clear, consistent, and delivered with warmth, children thrive. They learn that adults can be trusted to guide them, even when emotions run high.",
